<Site title="Kira, Privacy Policy" description="What the Kira Discord bot reads, stores and shares.">
	<section class="row">
		<article class="legal">
<h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
<p class="dim">Kira (Discord bot and its Activity). Last updated: 2026-10-10. <a href="#es">Versión en español</a></p>

<h2>Who runs this</h2>
<p>Kira is a hobby project run by one person (GitHub: <a href="https://github.com/snowarch">snowarch</a>). It is not a company and has no employees.</p>

<h2>What Kira reads</h2>
<p>Kira reads the messages sent in the channels where she is allowed to talk, and the direct messages people send to her. She uses them to answer. She does not read channels she has no access to.</p>

<h2>What Kira stores</h2>
<ul>
<li>Your Discord user ID and display name, and short notes about you that she writes herself (preferences, things you told her, how familiar you are with her).</li>
<li>Conversation turns: what you said to her and what she answered, with the channel and time.</li>
<li>Memories derived from conversations.</li>
</ul>
<p>This data lives on the owner's own computer. It is not sold, not used for advertising and not shared with other people.</p>

<h2>Third-party AI providers</h2>
<p>To write her replies, Kira sends the relevant part of the conversation (and, for that turn, images or documents you attached to a message addressed to her) to third-party AI model providers. Those providers process it under their own terms. Do not send her anything you would not want processed that way.</p>

<h2>The Activity</h2>
<p>The Kira Activity is a web page that shows her avatar and the last thing she said. It does not ask you to log in, does not read your Discord profile and does not set cookies or store anything in your browser.</p>

<h2>Retention and your choices</h2>
<p>Data is kept until the owner removes it. You can ask for everything Kira holds about you to be deleted by contacting the owner (see below), and you can stop at any time by not writing to her. Servers can remove the bot whenever they want.</p>

<h2>Children</h2>
<p>Kira is meant for people who are allowed to use Discord, which requires being at least 13 (or older where local law says so).</p>

<h2>Contact</h2>
<p>Open an issue at <a href="https://github.com/snowarch/inir-site/issues">github.com/snowarch/inir-site/issues</a> mentioning “Kira”, or message the owner on Discord.</p>

<h2>Changes</h2>
<p>If this policy changes, the date above changes with it.</p>

